    "updated_at": "2024-11-15T23:07:09Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the thoughts. So I've spent today implementing the \"throw\" behavior, and adding it to the spec. After doing that, it feels pretty natural, and seems to have fewer footguns than either \"no-op\" or \"fallthrough\". Both of those seem like surprising (and semi-silent) behavior, vs. getting an exception that tells you exactly why things are weird.\r\n\r\nBut please take a look at the new spec PR text https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10737 and also the updated set of tests [right here](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/6026242/1/third_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-dialog-element/dialog-requestclose.tentative.html), and let me know what you think.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
